From 33fe95ffaf029b46cc000efc32d5f2debde28b24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Garrett Brown <themagnificentmrb@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 00:22:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Skip empty disc slots when checking regions

New image slots have a NULL CDIF until populated. CalcDiscSCEx visited
those slots while replacing another image and crashed in CDIF_ReadSector.
Skip empty slots and clear their cached region ID.

MGS Debug-core regression:
- Before: adding two empty slots, then replacing slot 0, caused SIGSEGV.
- After: replacement, removal and no-disc restore pass with pending slots.
---
 libretro.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libretro.c b/libretro.c
index e7f85f62..58152217 100644
--- a/libretro.c
+++ b/libretro.c
@@ -2306,6 +2306,12 @@ static unsigned CalcDiscSCEx(void)
       unsigned i;
       for (i = 0; i < cdifs.count; i++)
       {
+         if (!cdifs.items[i])
+         {
+            cdifs.scex_ids[i] = NULL;
+            continue;
+         }
+
          uint8_t buf[2048];
          uint8_t fbuf[2048 + 1];
          char serial[BEETLE_DISC_SERIAL_SIZE];
